.TH GILLII 1 "2026-10-10" "gillii 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gillii \- restore cached WeChat mini-program packages and analyze APK files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gillii
.RI "list [--appid ID] [--root DIR]"
.br
.B gillii
.RI "clean [--appid ID] [--root DIR] [--dry-run]"
.br
.B gillii
.RI "info ID [--root DIR]"
.br
.B gillii
.RI "chase ID | chase FILE.apk [--output NEWDIR]"
.br
.B gillii
.RI "setup | version | help [COMMAND] | completion bash|zsh|fish"
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Bash orchestration tool using Node.js 22+ for V1MMWX decryption,
main-package extraction, restoration and static verification.
APK analysis additionally requires Python 3.10+.
APK analysis and extended reports are available since v0.2.0.
https://github.com/leo1394/homebrew-gillii
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Print only AppID and latest modification time, one row per AppID.
.TP
.B info
Show all cached packages for an AppID, including paths, versions, sizes,
modification times, cache roots and blocked paths.
.TP
.B clean
Permanently delete discovered .wxapkg files;
preserve other files and directories.
Quit WeChat first, then reopen only the target mini-program and run list.
Blocked paths or deletion errors cause a nonzero exit status.
.TP
.B setup
Copy bundled helpers to a user cache and install locked npm dependencies.
Requires npm registry access. Lifecycle scripts are disabled.
.TP
.B chase
Automatically select the newest readable main package, copy and restore it.
Release archives include dependencies; create ./ID-unique-suffix/source.
Failures preserve logs.
No business API requests are made.
An APK path selects Android analysis, raw extraction, ordinary Android
decompilation or Unity Mono export. Type-specific tools are prepared
automatically. Results include an HTML index and reproduction notes.
A complete analysis does not guarantee a buildable original project.
.TP
.B completion
Print Bash, Zsh or Fish completion without runtime dependencies.
.TP
.B version, --version
Print exactly two metadata lines.
.TP
.B help, --help
Print help; command-specific help is also supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --appid ID
An identifier of the form wx followed by 16 lowercase hexadecimal digits.
.TP
.B --root DIR
Optional cache search directory for list, info or clean.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Preview AppIDs and latest modification times without deleting files.
.TP
.B --input FILE_OR_DIR
Optional package file or directory; select its newest readable main package.
.TP
.B --output NEWDIR
Optional new output directory; parent must exist.
.TP
.B --
End option parsing. chase accepts its AppID or APK path afterward.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gillii list
gillii info wx0123456789abcdef
gillii clean
gillii chase wx0123456789abcdef
gillii help chase
gillii chase ./app.apk --output ./apk-result
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Mini-program cache root, default $HOME/.cache.
.TP
.B GILLII_NODE
Node executable, default node.
.TP
.B GILLII_APK_LAUNCHER_PYTHON
Python 3.10+ executable for the APK helper, default python3.
.TP
.B GILLII_APK_PYTHON
Prepared Unity Python interpreter with UnityPy and TypeTreeGeneratorAPI;
bypasses automatic Unity environment preparation.
.TP
.B GILLII_APK_CACHE
APK cache root, default $HOME/.cache/gillii/apk.
.TP
.B GILLII_APK_OFFLINE
Set to 1 to disable APK dependency downloads; use cached tools or overrides.
.TP
.B GILLII_APK_AAPT, GILLII_APK_DEXDUMP, GILLII_APK_JADX
Explicit Android inspection and decompilation executables.
.TP
.B GILLII_APK_DOTNET, GILLII_APK_ILSPY
Explicit .NET runtime executable and ilspycmd.dll path.
.SH FILES
Output includes original.wxapkg, decrypted package, raw/, source/, logs/
and report.json. Mini-program reports also include index.html, evidence/ inventories
and static API/config analysis, plus docs/analysis.md and docs/reproduction.md.
Selected package snapshots are kept together under packages/<AppID>/ for replay.
Dependencies are stored under the versioned user cache.
APK results include raw/original.apk, extracted/, evidence/, decompiled/,
unity-export/, docs/reproduction.md,
logs/, report.json and index.html; contents depend on the detected type.
.SH CAVEATS
macOS privacy may block terminal reads. Copy the AppID directory with Finder
and use --input. AppID paths and timestamps cannot identify an app by name.
Cached subpackages from the same version are merged. Uncached pages are
listed in report.json with status complete_cached. Games are unsupported.
Original variable names,
server code and runtime equivalence cannot be recovered or guaranteed.
Ordinary Android decompilation requires Java 11+ on PATH.
Automatic .NET setup supports macOS arm64/x64 and Linux arm64/x64; other hosts need
a compatible .NET 8 executable via GILLII_APK_DOTNET.
APK analysis initially targets macOS. Linux is unverified; Windows is
unsupported. Unity IL2CPP, Flutter and other native payloads produce partial
results, not restored source projects.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for success; 1 for invalid input, missing dependencies,
restoration or validation failure.
APK reports use complete (exit 0), partial (exit 2), or failed (exit 1).
Partial results preserve available artifacts and describe unsupported or
unsuccessful stages.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR node (1)
